<title>UK: UK's OFT to review Danka/Kodak unit deal.</title>
<headline>UK's OFT to review Danka/Kodak unit deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Office of Fair Trading (OFT) said on Tuesday it was considering if there was any need to investigate under UK merger rules the proposed acquistion by Danka Business Systems Plc of Eastman Kodak Co's Office Imaging Business.</p>
<p>The closing date for representations to the office is November 12, the OFT said in a statement.</p>
<p>Florida-based Danka said in September it would buy the Kodak unit for $684 million in a move that is expected to put it in a leading position in the fastest-growing segment of its market.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
